\frac{5}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383465} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b2eff7-7257-574b-910a-de8fb2777f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5b2eff7-7257-574b-910a-de8fb2777f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0f09f4-ea36-5762-a137-81e9d22e8820" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5274ce9-2e43-5d2e-b67b-78ba92b2c654" :question/math-academy-id "q-84080" :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{4}=2,\\,b=\\sqrt{100}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{10}{2}x \\\\  & =\\pm 5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
